1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,900
Hello again!

2
00:00:01,580 --> 00:00:03,320
Last time, we got stuck.

3
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:06,040
Do you remember what saved us?

4
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:08,080
The trick!

5
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:10,920
Take away a friend, and add five.

6
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:13,200
Today we learn all four.

7
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:14,020
Ready?

8
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:15,220
Let us go.

9
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:17,940
First, meet the friends.

10
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:20,280
Every small number has one.

11
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:22,960
Two friends that make five together.

12
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:23,780
Look.

13
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:25,700
One and four.

14
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:28,320
One and four make five.

15
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:29,880
So they are friends.

16
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:32,200
And two and three.

17
00:00:32,980 --> 00:00:35,240
Two and three make five as well.

18
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:36,240
Friends!

19
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,900
And that is all of them.

20
00:00:39,320 --> 00:00:40,340
Just two pairs.

21
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:42,980
Now you tell me.

22
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:44,960
Who is one's friend?

23
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:46,860
Four.

24
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:47,960
Well done!

25
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:49,620
And two's friend?

26
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:51,380
Three.

27
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:52,720
You have got it.

28
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:55,580
So three's friend is two.

29
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:58,060
And four's friend is one.

30
00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:01,580
Now watch what the friends do for us.

31
00:01:02,220 --> 00:01:05,540
To add one, take away four and add five.

32
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:10,120
To add two, take away three and add five.

33
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:14,520
To add three, take away two and add five.

34
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:17,260
Now you guess the last one.

35
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:22,620
To add four, take away one and add five.

36
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:24,200
Did you spot it?

37
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:27,860
The number we take away is always the friend.

38
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:30,020
Every single time.

39
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:32,400
Now, careful here.

40
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:34,220
This part is important.

41
00:01:34,940 --> 00:01:36,720
We do not always need a trick.

42
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:39,680
Always look at the lower beads first.

43
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:42,820
If there are enough, just push them up.

44
00:01:43,540 --> 00:01:43,800
Watch.

45
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:45,700
Two plus two.

46
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:48,040
Push two lower beads up.

47
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:50,000
Now push two more.

48
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:51,200
Done!

49
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:52,640
That was easy.

50
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:54,100
No trick at all.

51
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:58,100
But now try four plus one.

52
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:01,340
Push all four lower beads up.

53
00:02:01,940 --> 00:02:03,600
We want just one more.

54
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:05,040
Have a look.

55
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:06,480
Is there a bead left?

56
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:08,300
No.

57
00:02:08,660 --> 00:02:09,380
Not one.

58
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:11,920
And that is when we call a friend.

59
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:13,060
So.

60
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:14,940
One's friend is four.

61
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:18,900
That means take away four, and add five.

62
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:21,020
Remember our rule.

63
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:23,440
Lower beads move first.

64
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:24,980
So down they come.

65
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:26,760
All four of them.

66
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:29,340
Now the rod shows zero.

67
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:30,700
Oh no.

68
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:31,360
Zero?

69
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:33,140
Do not worry.

70
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:34,060
Watch this.

71
00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:36,320
Push the upper bead down.

72
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:37,960
And there it is.

73
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:38,700
Five!

74
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:41,420
Four plus one is five.

75
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:44,520
We wanted one more, and we got it.

76
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:46,800
Your turn to think.

77
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:48,480
Four plus two.

78
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:51,820
Clear the rod, and make four again.

79
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:54,120
Now, who is two's friend?

80
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:56,220
Three!

81
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:59,500
So take away three, and add five.

82
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:01,960
Down go three lower beads.

83
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:04,060
The rod shows one.

84
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:06,540
Now bring the upper bead down.

85
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:07,700
Six!

86
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:10,420
Four plus two is six.

87
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:12,100
One more.

88
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:13,720
Three plus four.

89
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:15,540
Clear the rod.

90
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:17,760
Push three lower beads up.

91
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:19,580
Now we add four.

92
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:21,780
And four's friend is...

93
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:23,160
One!

94
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:25,360
So take away one bead.

95
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:27,520
The rod shows two.

96
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:29,840
Bring the upper bead down.

97
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:31,140
Seven!

98
00:03:31,820 --> 00:03:33,560
Three plus four is seven.

99
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:36,320
You are getting fast at this.

100
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:37,640
Enjoying this?

101
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:40,800
Give this video a like, and subscribe for more.

102
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:43,120
Now stop and look.

103
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:44,620
Did you see it?

104
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:48,480
Every single time, we did the same two things.

105
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:50,120
Take away the friend.

106
00:03:50,860 --> 00:03:52,600
Then bring the upper bead down.

107
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:53,960
That is all.

108
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:55,560
The friend changes.

109
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:57,740
But the five never does.

110
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:00,560
Now it is your turn.

111
00:04:01,020 --> 00:04:02,000
All on your own.

112
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:04,480
Make two on your abacus.

113
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:06,140
Then add three.

114
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:07,120
Think.

115
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:08,980
What is three's friend?

116
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:13,480
Take it away, then bring the upper bead down.

117
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:16,000
What number is showing now?

118
00:04:17,460 --> 00:04:19,340
Two plus three is five.

119
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:20,720
Did you get it?

120
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:21,860
Well done!

121
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:25,880
That was the fourth friend, and you did it by yourself.

122
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:30,480
So now you know all four small friends for adding.

123
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:34,740
That is a real abacus formula, and it is yours.

124
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:38,120
Try them at home on your own abacus.

125
00:04:38,700 --> 00:04:42,880
Search for abacus kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

126
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:44,600
Download it free.

127
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:49,420
Next time, we will learn the small friends for taking away.

128
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:51,280
See you next time!
